Test-only: two fixes to QEMU 11.1.0's qemu-xhci (hw/usb/hcd-xhci.c) that
usbcom's split-cancel legs under xHCI98 found (2026-10-22-usbcom98-legs.md;
xHCI98 task 43.64), with a qtest.
1. Stop Endpoint saved QEMU's own fetch pointer as the TR Dequeue Pointer,
   past every TD it had fetched and cancelled ("FIXME ... data might be
   lost"), so after a driver rewrote a TD behind the head as a No Op and
   rang the doorbell (xHCI 1.2c 4.6.9, option 3) the live TDs ahead of it
   never ran again. xhci_stop_ep now saves the first TRB (and its cycle
   state) of the oldest fetched, not-completed transfer, as xhci_stall_ep
   already does for a halt (4.6.9: "pick up where it left off"). Stream
   endpoints are unchanged.
2. A No Op transfer TRB TD was handed to the device as a zero-length
   packet. It now completes Success (event if IOC) with no packet
   (4.11.7, 6.4.1.4).
Trace events usb_xhci_ep_stop_dequeue and usb_xhci_xfer_noop record both.
tests/qtest/usb-hcd-xhci-ring-test.c (qemu-xhci + usb-serial with no input,
which NAKs every bulk IN, a zero-length one too) checks the saved dequeue,
the No Op completion and the cancel-behind-head restart (with and without
data reaching the head TD afterwards); registered in
tests/qtest/meson.build for i386/x86_64. Applies to official QEMU v11.1.0
(on its own or after qemu-usbnet-hs.patch). Build as in
2026-10-23-qemu-xhci-cancel.md. The emulator remains GPL-2.0-or-later;
the files keep their upstream notices.

